+# NTSB request controls for Commission records and recorder attachments
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review. B129 / PD01–PD04, REC01 / REC02. The NTSB's released request-log compilation identifies the Commission-related control **FOIA-2010-00048** and recorder-attachment controls **FOIA-2009-00078** and **FOIA-2011-00215**. The latter was previously identified from a search preview. This review verifies its row against the downloaded page image. The case files, response letters and enclosures remain open. [NTSB request logs](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf)
+
+## What the register records
+
+Dates in the following table preserve the order and formatting of the register's separate columns. Page numbers refer to the full downloaded PDF. Line ranges in the source ledger refer to PyMuPDF's embedded text, which has OCR errors. The row values below were read from the page images.
+
+| Control | Scope in the description field | Received | Requested | Closed | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **FOIA-2010-00048** | Questions regarding the 9/11 Commission. The accident-number, date and location columns contain dashes. | 12/29/2009 | 12/22/2009 | 01/07/2010 | [PDF p. 40, printed 37/40](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=40) |
+| **FOIA-2009-00078** | Attachments to the digital flight data recorder specialist's factual report. The accident field reads **DCA01mA064**. | 01/05/2009 | 01/02/2009 | 04/07/2009 | [PDF p. 24, printed 21/40](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=24) |
+| **FOIA-2011-00215** | Attachment IV **757UALMap.xls** and Attachment III **DCA01MA065** tabular CSV files. The accident field also reads **DCA01MA065**. | 07/28/2011 | 07/28/2011 | 10/05/2011 | [PDF p. 74, printed 30/67](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=74) |
+| **FOIA-2008-00004-A** | Appeal of **FOIA 08-095**, seeking identification of the contents of pre-event FDR files for AA 77 and UAL 93, with 25 hours described in the request. The accident field reads **DCA01mA064**. | 05/20/2008 | 05/15/2008 | 05/28/2008 | [PDF pp. 3–4, both printed 1/40](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=3) |
+
+Both images of printed page 1 reproduce the selected appeal row. Count it once as a request control. The page header's selected fields include a closed date and omit an outcome or enclosure field. The closure dates support searches for the final correspondence. The rows leave grant, denial, referral, delivery, and file identity undetermined. The appeal description's 25 hours is requester scope, with actual coverage unverified. Likewise the generic Commission row leaves its precise questions and any relationship to the FAA May 2003 answer unknown.
+
+The separately reviewed Flight 93 factual report describes electronic CSV files and the data-frame map at physical p. 4. Its case context supplies a reason to pursue the named 2011 case file. The official report gives **757UALmap.xls**, while the request log prints **757UALMap.xls**. Preserve both spellings and seek an original manifest with exact filenames and hashes. The existence of either reference leaves the identity of the circulating CSV files unverified. [NTSB United 93 factual report, p. 4](https://www.ntsb.gov/about/Documents/UAL93FDR.pdf#page=4) · [2011 request row](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=74)
+
+## Conflicting fields and compilation boundaries
+
+- **FOIA-2011-00131.** The request description prints **9/11/2011** for reports concerning Flights 93 and 77. In the same row the accident-date field prints **9/11/2001**, and the closed-date field prints **09/06/2011**. Preserve all three fields. The submitted request and disposition could show whether the divergence originated in the request or in its log description. No determination was made. [PDF p. 69, printed 25/67](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=69)
+- **Letter versus bound copy.** The December 5, 2012 letter for **FOIA-2012-00232** describes a requests report from **9/1/2008 and 12/5/2012 (7 Pages)**. The 111-page public PDF separately contains two report title blocks dated **04/02/2013**. They describe requested-date periods **01/01/2008 and 12/31/2009** and **01/01/2010 and 12/31/2012** with printed totals of **40** and **67** pages. Physical pp. 3–4 are two images of printed 1/40. The relationship between the seven-page enclosure and the later reports in the bound copy remains open. Seek the original seven pages and the packaging or transmittal for the later reports. [Letter p. 2](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=2) · [Report title blocks pp. 3 and 45](https://www.governmentattic.org/12docs/FOIA_Logs_NTSB_2008-2012.pdf#page=45)
+
+## DOT checks and reading limits
+
+The DOT mirror titled 2007–2012 reproduces **Office of The Secretary of Transportation** search results. Its **2009-0243**, logged **07/24/2009**, describes a request about Northwest Airlines' response to the 9/11 attacks through December 31, 2001. It supplies a distinct request-control lead and leaves response status open. Its subject and custodian differ from the FAA correction investigation. [OST heading, PDF p. 2](https://documents.theblackvault.com/documents/foia/DOT-FOIALOG-2007-2012.pdf#page=2) · [Request row, p. 85](https://documents.theblackvault.com/documents/foia/DOT-FOIALOG-2007-2012.pdf#page=85)
+
+The DOT OIG cover identifies the accompanying log as calendar year **2016**. The embedded-text screen across all three PDFs returned no exact hits for **CC-2006-085** (including optional spaces and hyphens), **042R0122001**, or FAA request **2006005841**. This is a bounded screen of these copies, with scanned text and report filters limiting inference. The NTSB reports' date ranges differ from the August 2006 referral window. A missing join here leaves the location and outcome of the FAA referral unresolved. [DOT OIG 2016 cover, PDF p. 2](https://documents.theblackvault.com/documents/foia/DOTOIG-FOIACASELOG-2016.pdf#page=2)
+
+All three downloaded PDFs were checked for successful retrieval, file format, hash, byte length and page count on November 10 UTC. The screen covered 287 physical pages of embedded text and checked 26 fixed text anchors. Visually checked selected areas of NTSB pp. 2–4, 24, 40, 43, 45, 69, 74, 107 and 111 and OST p. 85. The visual review verified the selected rows and scope fields. The attached original data, independent decoder and clock-alignment work remain outside this acquisition comparison.
+
+## TODOs
+
+- [ ] **PD01–PD04.** Locate the actual **FOIA-2010-00048** request and dated response with any referrals. Compare its scope and enclosures to the FAA correction trail before linking them. The corrected May 2003 answer and delivery acknowledgment, signed action/no-action record, recommendation-specific disposition and applicable investigation and retention crosswalk remain open. [FAA disposition queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/README.md)
+- [ ] **REC01 / REC02.** Locate the determination letters, electronic enclosure manifests and retained delivery copies for **FOIA-2011-00215** and **FOIA-2009-00078**. Compare agency file hashes with the candidate copies. Keep **08-095** and **FOIA-2008-00004-A** separately keyed while seeking their original request, response and appeal decision. Do the exact-file comparison before attributing sample layout or apparent endpoints to an official release.
+- [ ] **PD01 / REC01.** Seek the actual **2006005841** transfer packet, receiving docket/control and media inventory. Keep the **2009-0243** Northwest Airlines case separate and check its response only if the scope advances an operational-record question.
